## Spatial and temporal transition map

| Window | Front | Living middle | Rear / residue | Required relationship |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 0–5 min | Cardamom capsule, polished rind, pepper/juniper | Terpinyl/linalyl shell and Bontoux lavender | First violet-metal and cedar glints | Cardamom remains first and lavender remains genetically attached |
| 5–30 min | Capsule contracts | Lower-pressure lavender exposes Jessemal/coumarin tissue | Leaf-metal stitches and root seams become legible | Shell must open inward rather than collapse into a separate sweet heart |
| 30–120 min | Aromatic seed residue | Coumarin, Tonkarome, tonka grain, heliotropal, immortelle, violet-suede cloth | Literal cedar/vetiver and Polysantol form around it | Warm interior must remain seed-like, not edible or iris-led |
| 2–6 h | Violet-root tailoring | Yielding wood and coumarinic skin | Cedar/vetiver verticality under bounded pressure | Tenderness and pressure must coexist without an amberwood wall |
| 6–24 h | Faint aromatic seed edge | Hayed almond and creamy skin echo | Pencil cedar and root residue | Late material recalls the cardamom-lavender subject without false top-note persistence |

All temporal statements are design intent, not observed evolution.

