Owned Lemon FCF and Cedarwood oil Virginia are not missing. Lemon is deliberately excluded from this night architecture; Virginia cedar is used in the current build. No recommendation authorizes procurement.

## Controlled blinded acceptance protocol

### Primary constant-total successor comparison

- Compare immutable V5.1 control against V6 at identical 6,000 uL concentrate and 20% finished concentration.
- Prepare two independent full-concentrate master sets on different occasions. Make duplicate coded pours from each master. Use anonymous randomized codes, balanced order, equal application mass, identical substrate, and a sealed key.
- Read free description first at 0, 5, 30, and 120 minutes, then 6 and 24 hours.
- Score 0–10: LNDL recognizability; cardamom leadership; lavender continuity; cold capsule clarity; warm crushed-seed plausibility; shell-to-seed continuity; violet-suede tailoring; literal cedar/vetiver verticality; yielding interior; airy/dense simultaneity; tenderness under pressure; spatial depth; late identity recurrence; overall liking; luxury/style.
- Score defects separately: lavender detergent; pastry/candy; lipstick iris; explicit leather; woody-amber wall; muddiness; harshness; sweetness; fatigue; intensity imbalance.

V6 advances only if LNDL identity is at least 6/10 and no more than one point below V5.1; overall liking is not lower; shell-to-seed continuity and at least one interior/base axis improve by at least one point; no drift defect worsens by more than one point; and both independent master sets show the same direction. If perceived intensity differs by more than one point, intensity-match and repeat. Discordant masters are `HOLD`, not averaged into success.

This paired successor comparison tests the **whole approved interiorization**, not the causal contribution of each of its nine dose changes. If it produces a repeatable difference, the free descriptions determine the next isolated constant-total arm. Do not run a nine-way screen or infer causality from the pair.

### High-value follow-ups only if implicated

1. **Pod velocity:** Cardamom EO 250/Terpinyl Acetate 200 versus Cardamom 230/Terpinyl 220, all else V5.1. This exact 20-for-20 swap isolates sharp capsule pressure versus slow pod depth.
2. **Lavender-air pressure:** V5.1 Bontoux 170/Linalyl 120/Hedione 220 versus V6 160/100/200, with the released 50 uL replaced by DPG. This tests whether reduced face pressure improves legibility before any interior reinforcement.
3. **Interior reinforcement:** only after the primary pair and pressure arm identify a gap, build a separate constant-total arm for Jessemal/Cedar/Vetiver/Polysantol increases. Choose the compensating matrix from the physical free descriptions; do not assume Benzyl Benzoate or DPG is olfactorily neutral without a control.

A null result is `NO DETECTED EFFECT AT THIS DOSE/PROTOCOL`, not proof of universal redundancy. Ingredient count remains hidden from evaluators.

## Claim ceiling

This artifact is a target-first theory formula and controlled experimental design. It has not been physically compounded or smelled. Passing parser, donor-independence, inventory, OAV, temporal, or release checks cannot establish similarity, liking, hedonism, luxury, completion, complexity, depth, three-dimensionality, safety, stability, diffusion, longevity, maturation, or commercial release.

